{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge","id":1051355,"title":"Arete 5/6 mage against a 5th or 6th Gen Kaldoun/Thautmurge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-18T21:27:00-08:00","id":1051355,"title":"Arete 5/6 mage against a 5th or 6th Gen Kaldoun/Thautmurge","content":"Hello there Onyxpath<br /> <br /> Not too long ago I was engaged in a conversation about the apparent power disparity between an arete 5/6 mage against a 5th or 6th gen kaldounic sorcery/thautmurge. The other person in the conversation was adamant that a Kaldounic sorcery, particular a 6th or 5th gen one, as well as a thautmurge could crush an Arete 5/6 mage in most cases. I said that it would depend on the mage, how prepared he or she was and so on.<br /> <br /> Question is, with little preparation or much preparation, how well do you think an arete 5/6 mage could stand up to such an adversary?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:45:59-08:00","id":1051360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge#post1051355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there Onyxpath<br /> <br /> Not too long ago I was engaged in a conversation about the apparent power disparity between an arete 5/6 mage against a 5th or 6th gen kaldounic sorcery/thautmurge. The other person in the conversation was adamant that a Kaldounic sorcery, particular a 6th or 5th gen one, as well as a thautmurge could crush an Arete 5/6 mage in most cases. I said that it would depend on the mage, how prepared he or she was and so on.<br /> <br /> Question is, with little preparation or much preparation, how well do you think an arete 5/6 mage could stand up to such an adversary?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> These are insane levels of difference. I mean this is everything from &quot;from naked human who just go up in the morning&quot; to post human cyborg god spaceship blasting sending wave after wave of killbots from orbit while shining sunlight on said vampire through mirrors for your mage its just not really a fair point..<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking the Mages have more potential options so its possible an Arete 5/6 mage will have something the Vampire just has no defense/plan for. Coversely with a more limited skill set the mage is more likely to have a counter/nosell for the vampire but this is the BROADEST strokes. Plenty of mages won't have the defenses or plans to handle what a 6th or 5th gen can throw at them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:07:00-08:00","id":1051368,"title":"","content":"Well, like you said, it depends on the mage. What Spheres they have, what mage group they belong to, what their Focus is, what resources they have (Wonders, Nodes, Familiars, etc). How much time we're really talking when we say &quot;little preparation&quot;. And what edition of the game we're using.<br /> <br /> On the other side, we need to know what Paths/Ways/Kraina the vampire possesses, and at what levels. What Clan they are, and whether or not they have something to establish to sympathetic connection to the mage with. What Rituals are they packing, and how much prep time they have to perform them. What they aim to gain from the conflict, and indeed how they are approaching this mortal magic user.<br /> <br /> With so many variables to consider, it's hard to determine how a conflict would play out. So let's just start throwing things out.<br /> <br /> If we're going with M20, a mystic mage would already have overcome the need for a few of their Instruments. They can throw out spells on short notice, and gain great advantage from use of the Instruments they've overcome (-1 to difficulty). If it's a technomancer, at Arete 6 they would just have overcome one of their Instruments, so they are slightly less versatile. A Technocrat cannot have overcome any Instruments at this time, so if he's caught flat-footed, without his tools, he may be screwed (though maybe not, if some of his Instruments are activity based, or internal to his body). If the mage can use Martial Arts as Instrument, they are in a position to face an attack well.<br /> <br /> If the mage has Correspondence 3, they are vastly less beatable. They could teleport away, and raise Wards against long-distance magic by the vampire. They could also turn the tables, using Correspondence to counter-scry on their opponent (using the connection formed by the initial assault), and even teleport over to attack the vampire directly. That is, if the mage cares to confront them in person. They could instead carpet bomb the vampire with any other Spheres they possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T02:12:46-08:00","id":1051433,"title":"","content":"Even an initial Mage char with enough creativity, the right resources and proper preparation could destroy the 5th gen vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T02:25:42-08:00","id":1051436,"title":"","content":"*stares at thread title*<br /> <br /> *braces for impact*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:02:19-08:00","id":1051499,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge#post1051355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there Onyxpath</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge#post1051355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not too long ago I was engaged in a conversation about the apparent power disparity between an arete 5/6 mage against a 5th or 6th gen kaldounic sorcery/thautmurge. The other person in the conversation was adamant that a Kaldounic sorcery, particular a 6th or 5th gen one, as well as a thautmurge could crush an Arete 5/6 mage in most cases. I said that it would depend on the mage, how prepared he or she was and so on.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Question is, with little preparation or much preparation, how well do you think an arete 5/6 mage could stand up to such an adversary?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051436#post1051436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*stares at thread title*<br /> <br /> *braces for impact*</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright... I'll run the first sacrifice to the pyre for this one...<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> The fundamental flaw-of-premise/misperception with this comparison (which goes back to the 90s with the now-old-school cross-comparisons) is in comparing a mage's Arete with an opponent's (a low generation vampire, in this case) &quot;x&quot; power. Neither the mage's Arete, in immediate context, nor the vampire's generation, alone, have any direct bearing metaphysically; rather, it's how well-developed their *expressions* of their innate power/potential is (i.e. how high a mage's rating in &quot;x&quot; Spheres are vs. how high said Koldun has developed his hedge magic). You can have a mage with Arete:7+ who doesn't have a Sphere above 3 or 4 (unlikely, but there are examples across the editions... and enough so as not to disregard the concept out of hand...); similarly, a 5th or 6th generation vampire could have been embraced last night and is only just manifesting his first/most basic abilities. Said 5th/6th generation vampire would have an powerful edge at levels 6+ in specific ways in which a *specific* power manifests vs. a mage who &quot;only&quot; has &quot;x&quot; Sphere at 3 or 4 (as a given power/ritual may well cover an (E)ffect that a mage can't compensate/cover for). On the flip, even some powerful rituals can be mitigated by a clever mage (particularly when using Conjunctional Effects) because of the flexibility and &quot;get-around&quot; that Magic(k)(tm) has over Hedge Magic(tm) (even very powerful Hedge Magic(tm) ). It's not quite so cut-and-dry as simply measuring things along one axis of power/determination.<br /> <br /> Short comparison: low generation vampires have a generally greater amount of potential &quot;oomph&quot; behind there juju (where applicable) due to their having Reality(tm) &quot;on their side&quot;, as it were, linked both to their connection to ultra-potent mythic threads as well as having Reality(tm) &quot;going along with them&quot; (if only subversively) when they &quot;do their thing&quot; (to paraphrase this relative to Mage cosmology). Mages, however, have inherently more potency and flexibility within their closer/more immediate potential (as their Spheres at 4/5 can do this, inherently and relative to potency, that even some of the strongest vampire hedge-wizards would be hard-pressed to match). Descriptors and indicated range-of-ability play as much a part in the assessment as the hard numbers do. A vampire with Dominate:4/5 can have his attempted mental influences thwarted viat Mind:1/2, assuming sufficient prep/successes; a particular blood ritual can circumvent the magic(k) of an Arete:10 mage if said mage doesn't have the proper defense in place and/or his world-view doesn't account for the way in which &quot;x&quot; occurs (assuming, of course, the mage has the appropriate Sphere(s) to counter/mitigate &quot;x&quot;).<br /> <br /> It's all relative. The math is just one part of the equation. The &quot;fluff&quot; is every bit as important in this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  bizarre cut/paste error 02-19-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:17:09-08:00","id":1051508,"title":"","content":"What about an elder thaumaturge/koldun/whatever with 5 in every path known to their brand of blood magic and pretty much any canon ritual (again known to their brand of BM) up to lvl 6 versus a Arete 6 Mythic (OoH, Cel Cor, Akhashic etc) mage with all Spheres at 5?<br /> <br /> The goal is to either kill the opponent or make their life so miserable that it isnt worth living.<br /> <br /> Each opponent have the full backing of their respective group (Camarilla/Sabbat and clan vs Tradition and the Traditions) in terms of resources but not extra manpower (plus whaterver peraonal resources an Elder/Master can personally possess).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T08:06:18-08:00","id":1051523,"title":"","content":"The mage stops time using that watch talisman that stops time. [insert elaborate series of precautionary things to ensure the vampire is deader than dead here.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T08:59:25-08:00","id":1051538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051523#post1051523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage stops time using that watch talisman that stops time. [insert elaborate series of precautionary things to ensure the vampire is deader than dead here.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... the Vampire gets a Wits + Occult roll to resist this, don't they? And any 6th Generation Koldun (of appropriate age) worth their salt has Occult 7 and Wits at 4 or higher. The resist roll is Difficulty 7, but I'm not sure if it's reflexive or something you need to consciously do. If it's the former the Vampire is screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T09:12:32-08:00","id":1051541,"title":"","content":"No they don't. It's not a curse on the vampire. It's an effect on the mage. They push themselves out of the timestream, then they do whatever they want before going back in. NORMALLY the downside is you can't do any magic while doing this. But that's why you use the Talisman. Because then IT'S fueling the spell not you.<br /> <br /> Giving the Vampire countermagick against that would be like giving the vampire countermagick against you buffing your strength score with life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T10:36:53-08:00","id":1051572,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter if they are mystic or Technomancer, the Mage with all spheres at 5 will have the capacity to No sell anything the Vampire throws at him. Contingency Spell plus all options is a hell of at hing.<br /> <br /> <br /> assuming a level of sublty the vampire can make the Mage's life miserable but.. then dies horribly when the Mage scries the cause. Bare in mind Mage with all sphere at 5 is pretty close to Omipotent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T10:46:53-08:00","id":1051574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051508#post1051508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an elder thaumaturge/koldun/whatever with 5 in every path known to their brand of blood magic and pretty much any canon ritual (again known to their brand of BM) up to lvl 6 versus a Arete 6 Mythic (OoH, Cel Cor, Akhashic etc) mage with all Spheres at 5?<br /> <br /> The goal is to either kill the opponent or make their life so miserable that it isnt worth living.<br /> <br /> Each opponent have the full backing of their respective group (Camarilla/Sabbat and clan vs Tradition and the Traditions) in terms of resources but not extra manpower (plus whaterver peraonal resources an Elder/Master can personally possess).</div> </div> </div> </div>The poor Vampire is doomed. Arete 6 with all spheres at 5?<br /> <br /> Not even the Twin sisters, the Matriarch of Mecha have that... Nor do ANY offcial Mage ever published (you have a few archmages like Porthos with 6+ in one Sphere, but NO ONE with 5 in all).<br /> <br /> Even 4th generations like Lazarus, Hardestat the Old, Etrius, whatever, would be fair game for such a Mage.<br /> <br /> You're talking about a guy that can build Etherships filled with Primium ALL BY HIMSELF, with proton cannons capable of atomic incineration, space/time distortion, fate manipulation, and much, much more<br /> <br /> Such a Mage can wouldn't go ALONE to fight anyone... He'll travel along his very Sanctum and Chantry to attack his enemy... In this case, the Mage will be fully assisted by a giant ethership, and inside his ship, he'll have his fully equiped lab. Inside his ship, an army of mutant creatures with a wide array of supernatural capacities... Robots, cyborg-hybrids and geneengineered can be sent on hundreds of capsules, plus several hundreds of hand-crafted spirits. The amount of Primium (or like substance) could render any static blood-magic into futile efforts, while a swarm of powerful monsters storm the house of the poor Vampire metuselah. Even fate would be against the Vampire - he can expect a huge unluck wave on his side, while his enemies are extremely luck. And, there is a high likelihood that a HUGE portal with an entrance to the Sun itself would be opened up INSIDE+ABOVE+BELLOW+SURRONDING the Vampire's house, pouring the pure plasma super heated energy directly from the Sun itself, every turn, no stop. And much, much more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T02:20:46-08:00","id":1051904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051508#post1051508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an elder thaumaturge/koldun/whatever with 5 in every path known to their brand of blood magic and pretty much any canon ritual (again known to their brand of BM) up to lvl 6 versus a Arete 6 Mythic (OoH, Cel Cor, Akhashic etc) mage with all Spheres at 5?<br /> <br /> The goal is to either kill the opponent or make their life so miserable that it isnt worth living.<br /> <br /> Each opponent have the full backing of their respective group (Camarilla/Sabbat and clan vs Tradition and the Traditions) in terms of resources but not extra manpower (plus whaterver peraonal resources an Elder/Master can personally possess).</div> </div> </div> </div>This Mage need not fight at all.<br /> <br /> He can easily set things up that you don't want/need/care to deal with him. Or that circumstances are against an attack every time. The Elder waits (time is on his side, or so he thinks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T02:47:31-08:00","id":1051911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051904#post1051904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This Mage need not fight at all.<br /> <br /> He can easily set things up that you don't want/need/care to deal with him. Or that circumstances are against an attack every time. The Elder waits (time is on his side, or so he thinks).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Or so he thinks&quot; indeed. I don't remember for certain, but I'm vaguely sure that by this point, the mage's Arete is high enough that he wouldn't even need to <i>roll</i> to predict the future. So let's just start there, and then realize (again) that our Master/Archmaster can stop time. A vampire has to advance Temporis - a rare Discipline to begin with - to high elder levels before they can pull that one off.<br /> <br /> What else would Mastery of all Spheres do for our hypothetical mage? Well, he can manipulate Entropy to the point where he's causing thoughts to be born and die as he chooses. Arguably, Entropy-based mental manipulation wouldn't even encounter the same sort of Willpower resistance that Mind-based ones would. The mage isn't touching the vampire's head directly, just shifting odds in their favor that thoughts problematic for the mage just...wither on the vine. The vampire could be made to forget what they were thinking about, and instead become fixated on other problems (and when you're a Methuselah, you have other problems).<br /> <br /> If the mage doesn't want to risk the vampire causing trouble for him or his loved ones down the line, he could always combine Correspondence 4 and Time 4, and displace the leech from space and time entirely. And because he's basically frozen in temporal stasis, the Koldun/Thaumaturge can't even attempt to unweave the enchantment. One moment he's in his haven, the next he's hundreds of years in the future. His resources are in worse shambles than if he'd taken to Torpor (since most vampires who feel the Torpor urge tend to have a chance to get their affairs in order). His ghouls are dead or signed on to different masters, and the power vacuum left by his absence has long since been filled, by rivals who have no intention of giving their gains back.<br /> <br /> And where is the mortal mage? Who knows? Might be dead, might have moved shop, might have built a Horizon realm beyond a vampire's reach. Might even have ascended. If the mage IS still around, he's had a few centuries to prepare for if (or when) the vampire comes back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T05:27:51-08:00","id":1051954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge#post1051355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I said that it would depend on the mage, how prepared he or she was and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd rarely take any other answer than this. These fights never take place in a vacuum and, even if they did, would give some inherent advantage to one or the other based on preferred fighting method.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T05:41:21-08:00","id":1051956,"title":"","content":"With Correspondence (4?) the mage could teleport the vampire to the day - side of the planet.<br /> <br /> With &quot;Path of antimagic&quot; (forgot how its called ) at 7 the vamp has a good answer.<br /> <br /> (Maybe &quot;Path of thaumaturgical countermagic&quot; perhaps...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:27:37-08:00","id":1051971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1051956#post1051956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Correspondence (4?) the mage could teleport the vampire to the day - side of the planet.<br /> <br /> With &quot;Path of antimagic&quot; (forgot how its called ) at 7 the vamp has a good answer.<br /> <br /> (Maybe &quot;Path of thaumaturgical countermagic&quot; perhaps...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Countermagic in VTM gives you a dicepool of 2x your rating in it against all forms of mystical attacks (blood magic, sorcery, Magick), but you only get your full dicepool (14 dice in this case) against someone whose magical techniques match with the method you've learnt to counter. So a Thaumaturge is 14 dice to resist Thaumaturgy, 7 to resist Necromancy, Magick, other forms of Blood Magic, Sorcery...<br /> <br /> There's no canon rules for pushing a Path above 5, I believe, so you might be stuck at 5.<br /> <br /> Also, the Vampire rolls at the difficulty the Mage casts with, so you will on average counter successes at a 1 to 1 basis, but each attempt costs a point of blood and must be conscious. Stack it with the Wits + Occult and give the Vampire decent Auspex and Perception, and they're counter-magick everything which tries to hit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:03:51-08:00","id":1051989,"title":"","content":"In VTM you need 2 successes of your countermagic dicepool to counter 1 Arete success, and the difficulty it's the Willpower of the Mage (an 8-9 would be typical for such a powerful Mage). As per the Vampire Storyteller's Handbook (revised).<br /> <br /> It doesn't &quot;stack&quot; to the Wits + Occult roll. M20 assumes that supernaturals don't have other way to counter (at least no other way it's mentioned, so one would assume this replaces all other Counter rules from previous books). At the very least, you should acknowledge that there are no rules saying that it stacks.<br /> <br /> Also M20 Counterspelling (the Wits + Occult roll) only works against things directed directly at you, and only if this isn't direct damage. It doesn't work against area of effect stuff, nor against spells directed at other people. I don't remember if VTM counter allows to counter indirect stuff<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an elder thaumaturge/koldun/whatever with 5 in every path known to their brand of blood magic and pretty much any canon ritual (again known to their brand of BM) up to lvl 6 versus a Arete 6 Mythic (OoH, Cel Cor, Akhashic etc) mage with all Spheres at 5?<br /> <br /> The goal is to either kill the opponent or make their life so miserable that it isnt worth living.<br /> <br /> Each opponent have the full backing of their respective group (Camarilla/Sabbat and clan vs Tradition and the Traditions) in terms of resources but not extra manpower (plus whaterver peraonal resources an Elder/Master can personally possess).</div> </div> </div> </div>This has...the same problems that before. Really, power wise, Spheres/Arete and Generation/Disciplines are inconmensurable. There's always ways for one to counter the other, and since these things don't happen in a vacuum it's impossible to know in advance. The Master may have any number of shenanigans in place, but then again, he may not. In the long run, all Spheres at 5 let's you destroy the elder in unlimited ways, but only if well used. Disciplines at 7-8 win the Sphere vs Discipline argument, but that's only IF the Sphere power it's directly countering a Dicipline or viceversa, a Mage has endless ways to asure this never happens, to make a defense/attack that dodges the opponent's defense/attack by simply being outside what the Static power can affect (like the Time 5 I Win button, best counter it's to assure that the Mage never presses the button).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-20-2017, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:48:28-08:00","id":1052003,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Short of rules saying that they don't stack, they must stack. Say a system has a rule for Dodging and Soaking, but never explicitly states that the two things work together. We are left to assume that since it doesn't say they don't stack, they must stack, unless they logically preclude eachother.<br /> <br /> Someone with Wits 9 and Occult 9 gets 18 dice to counter Magick (under special circumstances)... if they have Countermagic 1, do they get reduced to 2 dice? Or do they pick the bigger dicepool? What's their return on their investment in that case?<br /> <br /> Also, Countermagic explicitly states at higher levels that you can use it to inactivate any magic you can perceive. So you can reflexively protect someone else from a spell, as long as you have enough blood to spend. If you're 6th Generation you have enough blood to spend.<br /> <br /> So say a Mage attempts to use Mind to shield their mind from being read or controlled. Any Vampire with Auspex 6 or higher will sense their intent (a perfectly reasonable level 6 or 7 power) and can attempt to actively counter it in a reflexive roll using their Countermagic dicepool alone. That's 5 dice, and I was under the impression that the difficulty was 7, or the Mage's Arete, whichever is higher. 2 successes countering 1 success makes sense, but the Mage will be severely disadvantaged by the Vampire's &quot;soak&quot; against them.<br /> <br /> And if we're only using V20 rules (and we should), thaumaturgical countermagic is 1-to-1 success subtraction, and is rolled at an identical difficulty to the target's roll. So that, on average, means that the Mage is rolling as though they have 5 fewer dots of Arete, as successes will statistically speaking match successes. With Arete 6 or 7 they'll struggle to get powerful effects off of the ground, being limited to 1 or 2 dice. And RAW, if they use Quintessence to drop their difficulty our Vampire will lower their difficulty too, since that's the written rules for Countermagic in VTM (difficulties are equal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T08:52:57-08:00","id":1052021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of rules saying that they don't stack, they must stack. Say a system has a rule for Dodging and Soaking, but never explicitly states that the two things work together. We are left to assume that since it doesn't say they don't stack, they must stack, unless they logically preclude eachother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodging and Soaking are in the same book...these countermagic rules exist in a crossover section of two sepparate books, of two distinct gamelines, you can't assume that one was created with the other in mind.<br /> <br /> But let's accept both rules as valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone with Wits 9 and Occult 9 gets 18 dice to counter Magick (under special circumstances)... if they have Countermagic 1, do they get reduced to 2 dice? Or do they pick the bigger dicepool? What's their return on their investment in that case?<br /> <br /> Also, Countermagic explicitly states at higher levels that you can use it to inactivate any magic you can perceive. So you can reflexively protect someone else from a spell, as long as you have enough blood to spend. If you're 6th Generation you have enough blood to spend.<br /> <br /> So say a Mage attempts to use Mind to shield their mind from being read or controlled. Any Vampire with Auspex 6 or higher will sense their intent (a perfectly reasonable level 6 or 7 power) and can attempt to actively counter it in a reflexive roll using their Countermagic dicepool alone. That's 5 dice, and I was under the impression that the difficulty was 7, or the Mage's Arete, whichever is higher. 2 successes countering 1 success makes sense, but the Mage will be severely disadvantaged by the Vampire's &quot;soak&quot; against them.<br /> <br /> And if we're only using V20 rules (and we should), thaumaturgical countermagic is 1-to-1 success subtraction, and is rolled at an identical difficulty to the target's roll. So that, on average, means that the Mage is rolling as though they have 5 fewer dots of Arete, as successes will statistically speaking match successes. With Arete 6 or 7 they'll struggle to get powerful effects off of the ground, being limited to 1 or 2 dice. And RAW, if they use Quintessence to drop their difficulty our Vampire will lower their difficulty too, since that's the written rules for Countermagic in VTM (difficulties are equal). </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Sorry, you're right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-20-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:06:22-08:00","id":1052025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052021#post1052021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dodging and Soaking are in the same book...these countermagic rules exist in a crossover section of two sepparate books, of two distinct gamelines, you can't assume that one was created with the other in mind.<br /> <br /> But let's accept both rules as valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well M20 specifically gives Night Folk the Wits + Occult roll against Magick targeted at them which isn't externally formed (a fireball you make and then throw at them) or externally targeted (breaking the floor beneath them, turning sound into sunlight, teleporting the entire room to Australia). V20 specifically gives Vampires with Countermagic 5 10 dice against their chosen &quot;brand&quot; of magic (usually Thaumaturgy) and 5 dice against everything else, rolled at identical difficulty and rolled reflexively for 1 BP if they can see it coming, even targeting Magic which doesn't affect them or is more broad. There is nothing about either of these rules which contradict eachother, and they serve different purposes. The first rule protects The Prince from being turned into a Newt by a Mage. The second rule grants extra protection to those who have invested EXP in a specific Path of Blood Magic. Since they don't contradict eachother and they serve different purposes, they must stack.<br /> <br /> It would be different if the Werewolf rules said &quot;hurting Vampires with claws is -2 difficulty on the Strength roll&quot; and the Vampire rules said &quot;soaking Werewolf claws is +2 difficulty&quot;, since although those are different rules they are clearly intended to fulfill the exact same purpose and wouldn't be intended to stack, so you would pick one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:17:24-08:00","id":1052028,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:35:04-08:00","id":1052048,"title":"","content":"Outside Fiat rituals like Ur Shulgis generally blood magic has a &quot;you cast this it takes maybe a night and its done&quot;. Mage can make themself pretty unfindable for six months and spend that on &quot;Teleport Vampire into the sun&quot;/transform into lawnchair/etc<br /> <br /> <br /> This is before we get into &quot;Indirect&quot; targetting like &quot;I open a portal to the Sun above him while he sleeps&quot; Of course even more likely you can do stuff like Bless all his enemies to succeed against him, curse his ghouls so he can't function and he gets killed naturally...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:12:45-08:00","id":1052140,"title":"","content":"So... How many dice of countermagic does the Vampire have again?<br /> <br /> Well, let him counter 50 successes than...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:20:56-08:00","id":1052222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052140#post1052140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... How many dice of countermagic does the Vampire have again?<br /> <br /> Well, let him counter 50 successes than...</div> </div> </div> </div>I THINK the max would be letting people stack shenanigans 19 dice. That's his defense against being thrown into the sun.<br /> <br /> <br /> He has Zero Dice of defense against &quot;Open up gate way to the sun and a solar flare blasts through&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:18:55-08:00","id":1052253,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I find the idea of stacking any Thaumaturgical Countermagic dots on top of M20's innate countermagic is be absurd and broken. You either get the benefits of one or the other. Not both.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's what I would go with, were I the Storyteller running this hypothetical game.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the opinion that M20's rules on nightfolk countermagic shouldn't be automatic, like some kind of soak. It should be something the character has to do, <i>actively</i>. The Occult part of that roll is represented by the character applying their general knowledge of the supernatural in order to pull off some kind of protective action. Crossing oneself, brandishing a religious or occult symbol of protection, tracing a banishing pentagram in the air, throwing salt, clutching an iron nail, etc. Or using any of the thousands of folk charms, from gemstones to garlic, to resist the acts of sorcery. Like I said, this is not automatic, and, like with the Mages they are attempting to counter, they must dedicate their action to pulling it off. If we're going to be doing this &quot;innate countermagic&quot; thing, we might as well be fair about it.<br /> <br /> On another note, I checked my books again. It had this to say in its section on Nightfolk Countermagic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 p. 546</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the Night-Folk cannot counter immediate-damage attacks like plasma bolts or Enlightened martial arts, nor can they oppose indirect assaults like weakened floors, fire, typhoons, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while a Koldun or Thaumaturge could try to counter an attempt to kill him with Life 4 + Matter 2 or Prime 5, he'd still be vulnerable to things like fireballs, laser beams, or portals opened up to the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:27:18-08:00","id":1052258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052253#post1052253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I find the idea of stacking any Thaumaturgical Countermagic dots on top of M20's innate countermagic is be absurd and broken. You either get the benefits of one or the other. Not both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I gave him the benefits of both because.. all 5s in all sphere is insane. I'd even given him a full set of Doctor Doom Primium armor.. and he'd still lose. All sphere at 5 is just too damned versatile. Even with a perfect caveat of &quot;You cannot cast a spell directly on the vampire period&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 02-20-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:09:09-08:00","id":1052284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052258#post1052258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I gave him the benefits of both because.. all 5s in all sphere is insane. I'd even given him a full set of Doctor Doom Primium armor.. and he'd still lose. All sphere at 5 is just too damned versatile. Even with a perfect caveat of &amp;quot;You cannot cast a spell directly on the vampire period&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, the Mage CAN have the Doctor Doom full set of Primium with 10 counter magik, meaning that all thaumaturgical directly attacks will have to bypass that (yep, two can play this little &quot;countermagik&quot; game). Oh yes, and weapons of Primium can nullify Fortitute.<br /> Annnnnd... It won't be just the Mage with full sets of Primium right? The Mage can have golems, automatons, cyborgs, mutants, all those lab-made, fully hybridzed with Primium or Primium-like innate countermagik,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:38:22-08:00","id":1052331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052284#post1052284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention, the Mage CAN have the Doctor Doom full set of Primium with 10 counter magik, meaning that all thaumaturgical directly attacks will have to bypass that (yep, two can play this little &quot;countermagik&quot; game). Oh yes, and weapons of Primium can nullify Fortitute.<br /> Annnnnd... It won't be just the Mage with full sets of Primium right? The Mage can have golems, automatons, cyborgs, mutants, all those lab-made, fully hybridzed with Primium or Primium-like innate countermagik,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Mage doesn't really need counter magick on that level I can't think of any vector of attack on the mage that blood magic has that's not line of sight or material connection. Blood magic doesn't even let you do Scry and Fireball them through the scry... True magick does. The Mage can stay out of range forever and not be effected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T19:27:19-08:00","id":1052348,"title":"","content":"Forces 3 Prime 2 (Correspondence 2 optional) fill the immediate and surrounding environments with &quot;Holy&quot; Sunlight (unsoakable aggravated damage), since you have Prime 2 in the mix that sucker keeps rocking until you shut it down, throw in Matter 2 to tie it to the Vampires form and they can't run from it, even a reasonable Adept or Initiate (starting character) with the right spheres of study can End most Vampires on the fly, most moderately experienced Mages can easily do it (Forces 3 not just for Fireballs &amp; Flying, Matter 2 not just for turning old copies of USA Today in to stacks of Franklin's, and who doesn't pick up Prime 2 after the first story or two?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T20:05:21-08:00","id":1052358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052348#post1052348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...nd who doesn't pick up Prime 2 after the first story or two?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who haven't picked Entropy 2 yet<br /> Or Corr 2<br /> Or Time 2<br /> Or Mind 2<br /> Or Life 2<br /> Or Forces 2<br /> Or Matter 2<br /> Or Spirit 2<br /> <br /> Well... That's the thing about spheres... They are all just sooooo freaking good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:10:26-08:00","id":1052487,"title":"","content":"True but Prime 2 lets you do so much with making even simple effects permanent, Dead Presidents from Scrap paper (or polymer notes from chip packets) leaves a trail when the effect times out, but if it stays money you are still good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:35:57-08:00","id":1052495,"title":"","content":"You don't need Prime to make effects permanent, just lots of successes.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;multi master&quot; with all Spheres level 5... How much blood does a Vampire 5th gen have again?<br /> <br /> Because, with Time 4, Entropy 2, the Mage can let HUNDREDS of spells hanged... That he can unleash, all at once, with a single command.<br /> <br /> Just another thing that crossed my mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:46:50-08:00","id":1052499,"title":"","content":"Beyond countermagic I think the vampire has physical options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","user":"Colognian","date":". 02-21-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:16:18-08:00","id":1052553,"title":"","content":"There's a bajillon things a mage with all Spheres at 5 can do to kill a vampire bypassing all defenses and physical prowess that he may have.<br /> <br /> <i>However there's a small, but important, gap between being able to do something and actually doing it.</i><br /> <br /> The mage could appear in orbit with his super Ethership firing a load of antimater misiles to count chokula's castle, overwhelming all Countermagic and Fortitude, his army of Ghouls, his Castle, even fusing with the land wouldn't save him, as the land itself would be fucked. But then again, the mage might not have all that prepared, he might not know where his enemy it's (if he's in deep Elder level Obfuscation and attacks by proxy, as he should) or the vampire could have left the castle, with some serious Obfuscation and/or being protected by some Magick the he got from the mage's enemies, to plan a counterattack in the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-21-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:37:29-08:00","id":1052563,"title":"","content":"One effect suspended in time should be a last resort colocation. If anything would kill the mage it kills a colocated copy while the mage himself appears in his sanctum.<br /> (Correspondence 4, Life 3, Time 4, Entropy 2)<br /> <br /> It is a good thing to die...<br /> The elder thinks you dead (you should use you magick to thwart attempts to sense you).<br /> You can go on with your business or launch a surprise attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:53:31-08:00","id":1052612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052499#post1052499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond countermagic I think the vampire has physical options.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He has to get within range of the Mage which as a &quot;all spheres at 5&quot; is going to be pretty damned hard. Time 4. Contingency spell Correspeondence 3. Teleport. Setup contingency to &quot;Someone attacks me&quot; Magic goes off during intitiative. He's gone. Or contingency Time stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you a 5 of 6th gen with &quot;Every discipline they could possibly have access to reasonably&quot; so a Tremere with every path of thaum and the cardinal 8. a Tzim with Cardinal 8, Viscc, Obten, Koldunism or an assmite sorcerer with Cardinal 8, Duranki, and Quietus has alot more tools in the shead. But the major issue I keep seeing is the Mage can hit the Vampire at range and Vampire generally doesn't have stuff for throwing down like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even scary rituals like Chill of the Windsaber or Night of the Red Heart the Mage can just get out of the area pretty casually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Way of SPirit/Genius locii gives the Koldun some basic range but limits what he can throw at it.. and still doesn't have a handle on &quot;Guy is throwing magic at me from the far side of the globe&quot;(Or Mars)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:28:04-08:00","id":1052778,"title":"","content":"<b>Respawn</b> - Life 5, Mind 5, Spirit 5, Correspondence 4, Prime 2.<br /> The physical destruction of the body of the Mage doesn't mean <i>death</i>.<br /> Whenever the Mage's body is destroyed, this effect keep his soul connected to his Mind (Spirit 5 prevents his soul from shatter upon death, Mind 5 prevents his mind from dissolving, and keep the Mage as an astral form disconnected from his body).<br /> A special &quot;ressurection Chamber&quot; must be prepared for his return on the Mage's Sanctum. The Corr 4 in this effect will make the disembodied astral form of the Mage return to his chamber in his Sanctum, and Life 5 Prime 2 will give him a fully new body.<br /> <br /> <br /> There you go. This master can't be killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:49:39-08:00","id":1052797,"title":"","content":"Just a thought: How much paradox does the mage aquire in this conflict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:50:22-08:00","id":1052859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052797#post1052797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought: How much paradox does the mage aquire in this conflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>Zero if he is doing all that in his Sanctum AG his very own personal Horizon Realm (assuming no botches)<br /> <br /> Such a master wouldn't be &quot;casting on the go&quot; against the Vampire. Several effects hang out with Time 4, but mostly, the major part would be from talismans/devices. And, it would be made far away, on the safety of his Realm.<br /> <br /> (Don't forget that this guy can make Realms and can even manufacture nodes to feed it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:59:46-08:00","id":1052943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1052859#post1052859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Zero if he is doing all that in his Sanctum AG his very own personal Horizon Realm (assuming no botches)<br /> <br /> Such a master wouldn't be &quot;casting on the go&quot; against the Vampire. Several effects hang out with Time 4, but mostly, the major part would be from talismans/devices. And, it would be made far away, on the safety of his Realm.<br /> <br /> (Don't forget that this guy can make Realms and can even manufacture nodes to feed it)</div> </div> </div> </div>A Sanctum doesn't protect a mage from Paradox if the Effect in question goes <i>outside</i> the Sanctum. It's why mages can't use Correspondence to nuke all their enemies from safety.<br /> <br /> The REAL reason our hypothetical omni Master wouldn't have to worry about Paradox is because he has Prime 5. He can create a temporary Node anywhere, and can use the Quintessence from that to nullify any Paradox he gains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:21:41-08:00","id":1053050,"title":"","content":"You only get 1 paradox for every vulgar action, why do all of you act as if it's a death sentence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:36:45-08:00","id":1053057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1053050#post1053050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only get 1 paradox for every vulgar action, why do all of you act as if it's a death sentence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Backlashes used to be more common in Revised, as you instantly got one if you went above 5 total, and you got more than 1 point.<br /> Of course in M20, while only getting 1 point (sans botching), it will not immediately backlash but grow, and grow until you are possibly hit with the mother of backlashes.<br /> <br /> So, no, 1 point of paradox isn't bad. But try keeping those from piling up over time..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T02:23:04-08:00","id":1053105,"title":"","content":"We use a HR/clarification:<br /> When a suspended effect gets triggered in a vulgar manner then you gain Paradox. This way it is more consistent with Correspondence 4 and not so open to abuse.<br /> This way Paradox is indeed a concern in the above scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:04:27-08:00","id":1053173,"title":"","content":"Just use Prime 5 and a bit of your Nodes (yes, I said that in plural, because such a Master probably has several) to make Paradox a non issue...<br /> <br /> A fight between such a powerful Master and such a Vampire Thaumaturge it's probably going to involve a lot of people, time and resources. The real question it's not what can do the mage to kill the vampire, but rather how much of their vast resources they're willing to spend to do so. <br /> <br /> Still, I agree that killing someone that's hiding in the Horizon/Deep Umbra it's going to be somewhat chalenging for the Elder. That's why it's likely to be of supreme importance for the vampire to fight from the shadows, so the mage can't throw a ranged trump card before the leech can device a way to attack her enemy.<br /> <br /> Mages are far, far, better fighting with resources and distance than fighting hand to hand in an alley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:47:44-08:00","id":1053315,"title":"","content":"Altough a mage prepared to fight and willing to take Paradox head on is scary even for an Elder.<br /> One talisman and one Familiar can take up to 50 Paradox for the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:34:35-08:00","id":1053370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1053315#post1053315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altough a mage prepared to fight and willing to take Paradox head on is scary even for an Elder.<br /> One talisman and one Familiar can take up to 50 Paradox for the mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>50 paradox PER TALISMAN.<br /> <br /> Such a master will have hundreds of talismans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:49:36-08:00","id":1053377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1051355-arete-5-6-mage-against-a-5th-or-6th-gen-kaldoun-thautmurge?p=1053370#post1053370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 50 paradox PER TALISMAN.<br /> <br /> Such a master will have hundreds of talismans</div> </div> </div> </div>Well no, he wouldn't. Talismans need an investment of one <i>Permanent</i> Willpower point in order to finish. If it were an <i>Artifact</i> (functionally the same as a Talisman, but without its own Arete score, making it not usable by the unAwakened), he could make as many as he liked. But a Talisman is costly in a way that isn't easy to replenish. Even assuming that a mage can invest Willpower and raise the Trait again an unlimited number of times (so long as he has the XP to cover the cost), it's not likely for even our hypothetical Master to have done so too many times. Let alone likely that he'd WANT to, given that Talismans, having a shard of its creator's enlightened Will, have crazy strong connections to them for the purposes of Correspondence and other Sympathetic Magic.<br /> <br /> All of which is moot, since a Master like that would just create Periapts (Quintessence Batteries), which can hold considerably more Paradox than a typical Talisman, and can be left at Nodes to bleed those Paradox points off over time. If the Master had a fairly potent Periapt or two on them, they could go all out and only worry about putting them away after the immediate threat is dealt with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:13:11-08:00","id":1053387,"title":"","content":"If after 50 Paradoxpoints (in short order) the heat is still on, then a Master is certainly wise enough to retreat...<br /> <br /> Periapts can hold Paradox, sure. But it isn't explicitly stated that the Paradox goes into the Periapt before checking if an backlash occurs. Familiars and Talismans(for their creator) are able to do exactly that. (According to FbDF).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:52:22-08:00","id":1053793,"title":"","content":"Yup, it still helps to show how Paradox isn't such a limiting factor as some may believe.<br /> <br /> The battle it's going to depend on much subtler factors, like how the vampire and the mage chose to fight each other and the resources they can spend safely (without becoming target for the other mighty enemies/treacherous allies that they surely have)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}